hadiths[22]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18503","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Qays ibn Abbad, he said: I said to Ammar ibn Yasir: O Abu al-Yaqzan, do you see this matter which you undertook by your own opinion, or something the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entrusted to you. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not entrust to us anything he did not entrust to the people."
"18504","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Muradi, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, he said: Ammar said: When the polytheists lampooned us, we complained of that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Say to them as they say to you. He said: You would have seen us teaching it to the slave girls of the people of Madinah."
"18505","Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Najiyah al-Anazi, he said: Ammar and Abdullah ibn Mas'ud disputed about tayammum, so Abdullah said: If I remained a month and did not find water in it, I would not pray. Ammar said to him: Do you not remember when you and I were among the camels, and I became junub, so I rolled about as the beast rolls, then when I returned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of what I had done, he said: Tayammum would have sufficed you."
"18506","Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyah narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from the grandfather of his father al-Mukhariq, he said: I met Ammar on the Day of the Camel while he was urinating into a horn, so I said: I will fight with you and be with you. He said: Fight under the banner of your people, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to like for a man to fight under the banner of his people."
"18507","Quraysh ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar narrated to us, from his father, from Wasil ibn Hayyan, he said: Abu Wa'il said: Ammar addressed us and was eloquent and brief, then when he came down we said: O Abu al-Yaqzan, you were eloquent and brief, if only you had breathed. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The length of a man's prayer and the shortness of his sermon are a sign of his understanding, so lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermon, for indeed some eloquence is magic."
"18508","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ammar ibn Yasir, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was praying, so I greeted him, and he returned the greeting to me."
"18509","Affan and Yunus said: Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ammar ibn Yasir, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Yunus said: He asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about tayammum, so he said: One strike for the palms and the face. And Affan said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say regarding tayammum: One strike for the face and the palms."
"18510","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Tharwan ibn Milhan, he said: We were sitting in the mosque, then Ammar ibn Yasir passed by us, so we said to him: Narrate to us what you heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say about tribulation. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: After me there will be a people who take kingship, some of them killing others over it. He said: We said to him: If someone other than you had narrated it to us, we would not have believed him. He said: It will indeed happen."
"18511","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Khuthaym al-Muharibi narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Muhammad ibn Khuthaym Abu Yazid, from Ammar ibn Yasir, he said: Ali and I were two companions in the raid of Dhat al-Ushayrah, then when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, encamped there and stayed there, we saw some people of Banu Mudlij working at a spring of theirs among palm trees, so Ali said to me: O Abu al-Yaqzan, would you like to go to these people and see how they work. So we came to them and looked at their work for a while, then sleep overcame us, so Ali and I went and lay down in a heap of palm trees in fine dust, and we slept, and by Allah nothing woke us except the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, moving us with his foot, while we had become dusty from that dust, and on that day the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Ali: O Abu Turab, because of what he saw of dust on him. He said: Shall I not inform you two of the most wretched of people, two men. We said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The red man of Thamud who hamstrung the she-camel, and the one who will strike you, O Ali, on this, meaning his forehead, until this is wetted from it, meaning his beard."
"18512","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, from Ammar ibn Yasir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, halted for rest at the rear of the army, and with him was A'ishah his wife, then a necklace of hers of Zafari onyx beads broke, so the people were detained seeking her necklace, and that until dawn broke, and the people had no water with them, so Allah Almighty sent down upon His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the concession of purification with clean earth, so the Muslims stood with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and struck the ground with their hands, then raised their hands and did not grasp any soil, then wiped their faces and their arms up to the shoulders with them, and from the insides of their hands to the armpits. And the people should not be deceived by this. And it reached us that Abu Bakr said to A'ishah, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them both: By Allah, I did not know, indeed you are blessed."
"18513","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to me, from Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, from Ibn Las al-Khuza'i, he said: Ammar ibn Yasir entered the mosque and bowed two rak'ahs in it, making them very light and completing them, he said, then he sat, so we stood to him and sat with him, then we said to him: You made these two rak'ahs of yours very light, O Abu al-Yaqzan. He said: I hastened with them lest Satan enter upon me in them. He said, then he mentioned the hadith."
"18514","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, from Abu Mijlaz, he said: Ammar prayed a prayer and made it moderate, then he was asked, or it was said to him, so he said: I did not fall short of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"18515","Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Abu Hashim, from Abu Mijlaz, he said: Ammar led us in prayer and was brief in it, so they disapproved of that, so he said: Did I not complete the bowing and prostration. They said: Yes indeed. He said: Yet I supplicated in them with a supplication the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to supplicate with: O Allah, by Your knowledge of the unseen and Your power over creation, keep me alive as long as You know life is good for me, and take me when death is good for me. I ask You fear of You in private and in public, and the word of truth in anger and pleasure, and moderation in poverty and wealth, and the delight of looking at Your Face, and longing to meet You. And I seek refuge in You from harmful adversity and from misleading trial. O Allah, adorn us with the adornment of faith, and make us guides, guided."
"18516","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Khuthaym, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, Muhammad ibn Khuthaym Abu Yazid narrated to me, from Ammar ibn Yasir, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, and I were two companions in the raid of al-Ushayrah, then we passed by some men of Banu Mudlij working among palm trees of theirs, then he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Isa ibn Yunus."
"18517","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir, from Ammar ibn Yasir, that the Messenger of Allah said: Part of the fitrah, or: The fitrah is rinsing the mouth, sniffing water into the nose, trimming the mustache, the toothstick, clipping the nails, washing the knuckles, plucking the armpit, shaving the pubes, circumcision, and sprinkling water."
"18518","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, he said: I was sitting with Abu Musa and Abdullah, he said: Abu Musa said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, do you see, if a man did not find water, though he has been junub for a month, would he not perform tayammum. He said: No, even if he did not find water for a month. He said: Abu Musa said to him: How do you deal with this verse in Surat al-Ma'idah: Then you find no water, then seek clean earth. He said: Abdullah said: If they were given concession in this, they would soon, when water becomes cold upon them, perform tayammum with earth, then pray. He said: Abu Musa said to him: You disliked this only for that. He said: Yes. Abu Musa said to him: Have you not heard the statement of Ammar: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me on an errand, so I became junub and did not find water, so I rolled in the earth as the beast rolls, then I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him, so he said: It would have sufficed you to say, and he struck the ground with his hand, then wiped each one of them with its companion, then wiped his face with them. Al-A'mash did not go beyond the palms. He said: Abdullah said to him: Have you not seen Umar was not convinced by the statement of Ammar."
"18519","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Sulayman al-A'mash narrated to us, Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: I was sitting with Abdullah and Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, then Abu Musa said to Abdullah: If a man did not find water, he would not pray. Abdullah said: No. Abu Musa said: Do you not remember when Ammar said to Umar: Do you not remember when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me and you regarding camels, and I was afflicted with janabah, so I rolled in dust, then when I returned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I informed him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laughed and said: It would have sufficed you to say like this, and he struck the ground with his palms, then wiped his palms together and wiped his face one wipe with one strike. Abdullah said: Certainly, I did not see Umar convinced by that. He said: Abu Musa said to him: What about this verse in Surat al-Nisa: Then you find no water, then seek clean earth. He said: Abdullah did not know what to say, and said: If we gave them concession in tayammum, one of them, if cold water touches his skin, would soon perform tayammum. Affan said: Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, rejected it, so I asked Hafs ibn Ghiyath, so he said: Al-A'mash used to narrate it to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, and he mentioned Abu Wa'il."
"18520","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Wa'il, he said: Abu Musa said to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: If we do not find water, we do not pray. He said: Abdullah said: Yes, if we do not find water for a month, we do not pray, and if I gave them concession in this, when one of them feels cold, he would say like this, meaning perform tayammum, and pray. He said: I said to him: Where is the statement of Ammar to Umar. He said: I did not see Umar convinced by the statement of Ammar."
"18521","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il say: When Ali sent Ammar and al-Hasan to Kufah to rouse them, Ammar addressed, so he said: I know indeed that she is his wife in this world and the Hereafter, but Allah Almighty has tested you, whether you follow Him or her."
"18522","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Dharr, from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, that a man came to Umar and said: I became junub and did not find water. Umar said: Do not pray. Ammar said: Do you not remember, O Commander of the Believers, when you and I were in a detachment, and we became junub and did not find water, as for you, you did not pray, and as for me, I rolled in dust and prayed, then when we came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I mentioned that to him, so he said: It would have sufficed you. And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, struck the ground with his hand, then blew into it and wiped his face and his palms with it."
"18523","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Dharr, from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, that a man came to Umar, then Ibn Ja'far mentioned the like of the hadith of al-Hakam, and added: He said: And Salamah doubted, he said: I do not know whether he said in it: the elbows or up to the palms. Umar said: Yes indeed, we entrust you with what you undertook."
"18524","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, he said: I was sitting with Abdullah and Abu Musa, then Abu Musa said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, a man becomes junub and does not find water, should he pray. He said: No. He said: Have you not heard the statement of Ammar to Umar: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us, you and me, then I became junub and rolled in the earth, then we came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him, so he said: Like this would have sufficed you, and he wiped his face and his palms once. He said: I did not see Umar convinced by that. He said: How do you deal with this verse: Then you find no water, then seek clean earth. He said: If we gave them concession in this, one of them, when he finds cold water, would wipe with earth. Al-A'mash said: I said to Shaqiq: He disliked it only for this."
